  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking changes:\n- Casting a string to Bcp47KeyedSubtag throws InvalidCastException unless it is one extension or one private use sequence.\n- Loading a `SubtagRegistry` throws `FormatException`, naming the record's line, for a `Prefix` that isn't a well-formed language tag or that repeats a variant subtag or extension singleton, a `Suppress-Script` that isn't a script subtag, a `Macrolanguage` that isn't a primary language subtag, a `Preferred-Value` not in the form RFC 5646 §3.1.2 gives it for the record's `Type`, an `extlang` record whose `Preferred-Value` is missing or not identical to its `Subtag`, and an empty `Suppress-Script`, `Macrolanguage` or `Preferred-Value` (RFC 5646 §2.2.2, §2.2.9, §3.1.2, §3.1.7 to §3.1.10). Before, such a registry loaded.\n- `Bcp47KeyedSubtag.Singleton` returns `char` instead of `char?`; code that reads `.Value` or `.HasValue`, or applies `??` to it, uses the property directly.\n\nFixed:\n- A reused `Bcp47LanguageTagBuilder` no longer returns the earlier tag, or mixes the earlier tag's subtags into the new one. `UsingLanguageTag` and `UsingPrimaryLanguageSubtag` each start a new tag; the Subtag Registry or conformance chosen stays.\n- Loading a `SubtagRegistry` throws `FormatException`, naming the line, for a `Prefix` field outside an `extlang` or `variant` record, an `extlang` record without exactly one, an empty `Prefix` or `Scope`, a `Suppress-Script`, `Macrolanguage` or `Scope` field outside a `language` or `extlang` record, a `Scope` other than `macrolanguage`, `collection`, `special` and `private-use`, a `Subtag` that isn't a subtag of its record's `Type` in the case RFC 5646 §3.1.4 gives it, a `Tag` not formatted as §2.1.1 describes, or a character outside printable US-ASCII in a field RFC 5646 defines, other than `Description` and `Comments` (RFC 5646 §3.1.1, §3.1.2, §3.1.4, §3.1.8). Before, such a registry loaded and its records showed up through `Languages`, `Regions`, `TryGetSubtag` and the other members.\n- Bcp47LanguageTag.Create with LanguageTagConformance.IsoCodeLists reports a repeated variant subtag or extension singleton with its own message, instead of blaming well-formedness or the ISO code lists.\n- The package now includes its XML documentation, so IntelliSense shows member descriptions.\n- Parsing a language tag, and `Bcp47LanguageTagBuilder.UsingVariantSubtags`, check a long list of variant subtags for repeats faster.",
